 "method": "Doors audited: every row of validation/doors.json (the map's doors, with their states) plus every portal in the placed rooms' own contracts\n(sources/<room>/contracts/interface.json), placed with the room instance's transform; internal portals included (they show cut-outs inside a room).\nMethod: from the door plane, rays along the door normal to both sides (start 0.35 m off the plane so the door's own leaves and frame are skipped, up to 8 m),\nat three points across the middle of the door (centre and +-min(0.3 w, 0.9 m): a player with margin) and two heights (1.0 m and 1.7 m, capped below the clear height); the clear depth of a side is the\nshortest of its six rays plus 0.35 m. Every evaluated mesh, curve and text triangle counts (instances included; COLLIDERS, haze and volume boxes excluded).\nVerdicts: an open door or internal portal needs >= 1.2 m on both sides; a closed or emergency exit needs >= 1.5 m outside (a door that opens onto less is a\ndoor staring into a wall). Doors wider than 3 m are also probed at +-0.3 w and reported as \"narrows\" when the full width meets a wall\nwithin 1.2 m (a wide frame onto a narrower passage: information, not a fail). Geometry only: it does not know what a player should see behind a door.",
 "thresholds": {
  "open_min_m": 1.2,
  "exit_min_m": 1.5,
  "skip_m": 0.35,
  "reach_m": 8.0
 },
